The sign-ins step of the Arc import (plan 04 M2). After a profile's
sidebar import, it reads a copy of that Arc profile's cookie database, decodes
it with the key derived from Arc's "Arc Safe Storage" Keychain item (asked for
once per import, only after the user chose to bring sign-ins over), and writes
the cookies into the rac profile through the cookie writer. Non-default Arc
profiles become new rac profiles, reused on later imports. Arc must be quit
first. Only one Arc import, Undo or retry runs at a time. The import screens'
backend reports the step on macOS and uses the real Arc-running check, quit
watcher and sign-ins retry; the page still has to show the sign-ins result,
the quit-Arc gate and the retry button (UI).

